[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3905259744","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116333#issuecomment-3905259744","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116333","id":3905259744,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7oxYjg","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-15T21:59:45Z","updated_at":"2026-02-15T21:59:45Z","body":"Quick first impressions:\r\n\r\n- These look like decent improvement numbers, but please post the exact benchmarks you ran so maintainers can check the performance improvement.\r\n- More than 5 signals connected sounds rare to me. What's the reason you're optimizing this? \r\n\r\nThe early outs added do make sense to me since they should be pretty cheap and occur often enough to be worth doing.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3905259744/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3905281153","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116333#issuecomment-3905281153","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116333","id":3905281153,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7oxdyB","user":{"login":"killerdevildog","id":31830590,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODMwNTkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31830590?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog","html_url":"https://github.com/killerdevildog","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-15T22:15:24Z","updated_at":"2026-02-15T22:15:24Z","body":"@Ivorforce\r\nMy intention is to use this in my custom build for a project I'm working on—a procedurally generated open-world survival game where players can build massive structures and simulate complex ecosystems. It really needs that performance boost to handle all the dynamic elements without lagging, especially on mid-range hardware. I figured it could be helpful for anyone else tackling similar high-demand projects.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3905281153/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3905301894","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116333#issuecomment-3905301894","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116333","id":3905301894,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7oxi2G","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-15T22:31:15Z","updated_at":"2026-02-15T22:32:23Z","body":"So your design requires attaching lots of observers to single signals? \r\nI'm asking because this is the only sort-of controversial change for me. By increasing the number of stack-handled signals, we're improving performance for observer counts 5 to 16, but decreasing performance for all other observer counts.\r\nSo I need to understand where it's coming from and if you have measured it to be a bottleneck with a profiler.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3905301894/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3905951571","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116333#issuecomment-3905951571","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116333","id":3905951571,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7o0BdT","user":{"login":"killerdevildog","id":31830590,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODMwNTkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31830590?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog","html_url":"https://github.com/killerdevildog","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-16T01:20:47Z","updated_at":"2026-02-16T01:20:47Z","body":"@Ivorforce Thanks for the review and the pointed question.\r\n\r\nYou're right to push back on `MAX_SLOTS_ON_STACK`. I don't have profiler data showing 6-16 connection signals as a measured bottleneck in a real project just yet — the improvement there showed up in a synthetic micro-benchmark (10-connection signal emit went from ~603k to ~820k ops/sec), but that's not representative of typical usage.\r\n\r\nI'm happy to drop the `MAX_SLOTS_ON_STACK` change and keep this PR focused on the two changes you already find reasonable:\r\n\r\n1. **Early-out for empty `slot_map`** — avoids entering the copy/dispatch path when a signal has zero connections.\r\n2. **`has_one_shots` flag to skip the disconnection loop** — tracks during the copy loop with a single bitwise OR, then guards the second scan with `unlikely()`. Zero cost when there are one-shots, saves a full `slot_count` iteration when there aren't.\r\n\r\nHere are the benchmark numbers I measured (Linux x86_64, `scons target=editor tests=yes`, doctest harness using `OS::get_ticks_usec()`):\r\n\r\n| Benchmark | Before (ops/sec) | After (ops/sec) | Change |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| Signal emit, 1 connection | 5,487,570 | 6,238,692 | +13.7% |\r\n| Signal emit, 10 connections | 602,750 | 819,840 | +36.0% |\r\n| Simulated frame (100 objects) | 5,128,468 | 5,668,612 | +10.5% |\r\n\r\nThe 10-connection improvement is largely from the stack increase, so those numbers would be smaller with `MAX_SLOTS_ON_STACK` left at 5. The 1-connection and simulated frame improvements come primarily from the early-out and one-shot skip.\r\n\r\nWant me to push an updated commit with `MAX_SLOTS_ON_STACK` reverted to 5?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3905951571/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3906019607","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116333#issuecomment-3906019607","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116333","id":3906019607,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7o0SEX","user":{"login":"ryevdokimov","id":105675984,"node_id":"U_kgDOBkx80A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105675984?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov","html_url":"https://github.com/ryevdokimov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-16T01:40:33Z","updated_at":"2026-02-16T01:40:33Z","body":"Replying using AI doesn't really help lend credence that those benchmarks weren't entirely hallucinated by whatever prompt you seem to have copy pasted.  ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3906019607/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3906035913","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116333#issuecomment-3906035913","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116333","id":3906035913,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7o0WDJ","user":{"login":"killerdevildog","id":31830590,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODMwNTkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31830590?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog","html_url":"https://github.com/killerdevildog","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-16T01:45:50Z","updated_at":"2026-02-16T01:45:50Z","body":"> Replying using AI doesn't really help lend credence that those benchmarks weren't entirely hallucinated by whatever prompt you seem to have copy pasted.\r\nI believe this is off topic, I use ai to help format and help me communicate clearer, and for filtering my communication to remain on topic. This data is a real benchmark I used with a custom benchmark tool. \r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3906035913/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3906047978","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116333#issuecomment-3906047978","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116333","id":3906047978,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7o0Y_q","user":{"login":"ryevdokimov","id":105675984,"node_id":"U_kgDOBkx80A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105675984?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov","html_url":"https://github.com/ryevdokimov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.git