tions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-16T02:03:20Z","updated_at":"2026-02-16T08:52:45Z","body":"> Good idea, better yet we can both just run autonomous agents that will communicate with each other without our intervention, and things will just work out.\r\n\r\nThis is a brilliant Idea\r\nMore like: user → user’s agent → other user’s agent → other user.\r\nThe agents act as translation/clarification layers so the humans get a clearer message and fewer misunderstandings.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3906078475/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":1,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"off-topic"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3907205207","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116333#issuecomment-3907205207","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116333","id":3907205207,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7o4zhX","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-16T08:56:59Z","updated_at":"2026-02-16T08:59:37Z","body":"@killerdevildog Please note that we have a rule for [AI assisted contributions](https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/pull_requests/pull_request_guidelines.html#ai-assisted-contributions) — you are required to disclose what you are using AI for. If you are using AI to write parts of your messages and pull request description, you should disclose this. If you were using AI to write part of your code, or benchmarks, you should disclose this.\r\n\r\nYou also have ignored my request to post the benchmarks code you ran, please rectify this and post the benchmarks.\r\n\r\n> Want me to push an updated commit with MAX_SLOTS_ON_STACK reverted to 5?\r\n\r\nIf you have profile data of your game that shows 5-16 connections to be a bottleneck, please post it and we can consider this change. Otherwise, yes, please remove this change.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3907205207/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":6,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3909642852","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116333#issuecomment-3909642852","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116333","id":3909642852,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7pCGpk","user":{"login":"killerdevildog","id":31830590,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODMwNTkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31830590?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog","html_url":"https://github.com/killerdevildog","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-16T17:14:43Z","updated_at":"2026-02-16T17:14:43Z","body":"@Ivorforce Thank you for the feedback and for pointing out the contribution guidelines—I appreciate you taking the time to review this.\n\nRegarding the benchmark code: I apologize if it seemed like I ignored your request. In my earlier response, I shared the numbers from the benchmarks I ran using a custom tool with OS::get_ticks_usec(), but I haven't posted the full code yet. I'll work on uploading that shortly to provide full transparency.\n\nOn the MAX_SLOTS_ON_STACK change: As I mentioned before, \"I don't have profiler data showing 6-16 connection signals as a measured bottleneck in a real project just yet.\" Since I don't have that data right now, I'll go ahead and remove this change from the PR to keep things focused. We can always revisit it in a future PR if profiling shows it's worthwhile.\n\nAs for AI usage: AI was consulted and used to help create parts of the code, as well as to assist with formatting and clarifying my communications. I've reviewed and tested everything myself to ensure it's accurate and functional, in line with the guidelines. If you'd like to know more about my stance on using AI in programming, you can read about it in my Contributions repo here: https://github.com/killerdevildog/Contributions.\n\nThanks again for your guidance—looking forward to your thoughts on the updated commit after I get it done later today. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3909642852/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3910687031","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116333#issuecomment-3910687031","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116333","id":3910687031,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7pGFk3","user":{"login":"killerdevildog","id":31830590,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODMwNTkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31830590?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog","html_url":"https://github.com/killerdevildog","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/killerdevildog/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-16T22:03:44Z","updated_at":"2026-02-16T22:03:44Z","body":"[benchmark_tools.patch](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25350242/benchmark_tools.patch)\r\n\r\n\r\n@Ivorforce Here's the benchmark tooling and results I used to measure the improvement. I've attached a patch file (`benchmark_tools.patch`) that contains everything needed to reproduce:\r\n\r\n**What's in the patch:**\r\n\r\n- `tests/benchmarks/test_benchmark.h` — A doctest-based benchmark suite (38 test cases) covering Variant construction, signal emission, Object::get(), StringName ops, container performance (List/Vector/LocalVector), math ops (Vector3/Basis/Transform3D), and a simulated frame workload. Uses `OS::get_ticks_usec()` for timing with `do_not_optimize()` barriers to prevent compiler elimination.\r\n- `tests/benchmarks/run_benchmarks.sh` — Runner script that captures system info and saves timestamped results.\r\n- `tests/test_main.cpp` — One-line addition to include the benchmark header.\r\n- `tests/benchmarks/baseline_master_results.txt` — Full results from `master` (commit `bf95b62586`).\r\n- `tests/benchmarks/optimized_results.txt` — Full results from this PR branch.\r\n\r\n**How to reproduce:**\r\n\r\n```bash\r\ngit apply benchmark_tools.patch\r\nscons platform=linuxbsd target=editor tests=yes -j16\r\n[godot.linuxbsd.editor.x86_64](http://_vscodecontentref_/0) --headless --test --test-case=\"*[Benchmark]*\" --success","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3910687031/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4760587511","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116333#issuecomment-4760587511","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116333","id":4760587511,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABG8DM9w","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"http